  <DataPropertyAssertion><DataProperty abbreviatedIRI="kt:description"/><NamedIndividual abbreviatedIRI="kt:rr-transitive-nondeterministic-merge"/><Literal>Reduced fuzz seed 106255: t transitive with inverse ti, x4 in {x3,x5}, t(x0,x2), t(x2,x5), t(x5,x4) and g(x2,x3): x3 has no entailed ti-target, t(x0,x3) only holds in the models with x4 = x3. The marker propagation test of the role realization continued the cached consistency model, in which x3 was merged into x4 by a choice, added the propagation concept to that node independently of the merge and reported x2 and x0 as deterministic ti-targets of x3 (unsound; fixed in 9bdc7997: the candidates are only possible instances if the testing individual is non-deterministically merged). The t-targets of x0 and x2 are controls.</Literal></DataPropertyAssertion>
